# 5. Important Aadhaar Authentication Constraint

The application UI will use the **Aadhaar number as the patient's identity identifier** and an OTP-based verification flow.

However, the prototype must not pretend that it can independently verify Aadhaar ownership merely by sending an arbitrary SMS OTP.

Actual Aadhaar authentication/e-KYC requires an authorized UIDAI ecosystem/provider.

Therefore:

### Prototype

Use:

```text
Aadhaar Number
        ↓
Registered Mobile Number
        ↓
OTP
        ↓
Verification
        ↓
Create/Login Patient
```

The OTP provider may be a development/mock service during the prototype.

### Production

The authentication layer must be replaced with an authorized Aadhaar/UIDAI-compatible service.

The rest of the application must not depend directly on the Aadhaar provider.

